<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Vaghela dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">1244 CE – 1304 CE (approx.) · capital Anahilavada</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The last Hindu dynasty of Gujarat, ruling from Anahilavada until Alauddin Khalji's conquest at the start of the 14th century.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghel">Vaghelas</a> were a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chaulukya-dynasty">Chaulukyas of Gujarat</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lavanaprasada">Lavanaprasada</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viradhavala">Viradhavala</a>, as ministers and generals, held real power under the last Chaulukya kings from the early 13th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vigraharaja-iv">Visaladeva</a> took the throne at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a> (Patan) around 1244, formally founding the Vaghela dynasty.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The ministers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vastupala">Vastupala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tejapala">Tejapala</a>, serving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viradhavala">Viradhavala</a>, are famous for building Jain temples at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-abu">Mount Abu</a>, notably the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luna-vasahi">Luna Vasahi</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilwara-temples">Dilwara</a>, and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girnar">Girnar</a> and for their patronage of literature. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat's</a> ports, notably <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khambhat">Cambay</a>, traded across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. The kings fought the Paramaras, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/seuna-yadava-dynasty">Seuna Yadava dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1299 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alauddin-khalji">Alauddin Khalji's</a> generals <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulugh-khan">Ulugh Khan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nusrat-khan">Nusrat Khan</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-gujarat">Anahilavada</a>; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karna-vaghela">Karna</a> fled and his queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamala-devi">Kamala Devi</a> was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a>. Karna held out in the south until about 1304, when Gujarat became a province of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1244 CE – 1304 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.46%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1244 CE – 1304 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Anahilavada</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Visaladeva, Sarangadeva, Karna</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism, Jainism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Sanskrit, Old Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vaghelas of Gujarat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1274&amp;focus=vaghela-dynasty" aria-label="Vaghela dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6798 1387 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vaghela dynasty